# Freshservice update

## Gate

Update **only** when the user names an existing ticket (id / display id) or
explicitly says to revise / refresh / comment on a known Freshservice ticket.

Do not invent a ticket id. Resolve via connected MCP search/get when ready,
or the operator’s configured API/UI path. Ambiguity → ask once for the id, or
stop.

## Prefer additive updates

1. Read the current ticket so subject, type, status, and description are known.
2. Prefer a **note / reply / public or private comment** for progress chatter
   and evidence — leave the durable description stable when possible.
3. Edit the description only when the user asked to fix shape, correct facts,
   or replace a stub — then follow `freshservice-ticket`.
4. Never delete fields, custom attributes, or attachments you do not
   understand.

## Field discipline

- Subject: keep stable unless the user asked to rename.
- Type: do not convert Incident ↔ Change unless the user named the new type
  and the workspace allows it.
- Priority / group / requester: `freshservice-status` honesty — named or
  existing only.
- Links: add related ids the user named; do not invent.

## Status during update

Status changes are a separate authorization from “add a note”:

- “Update the ticket with X” → note/description only unless they also said
  resolve / close / assign / pending.
- Resolve/close still needs evidence (`freshservice-status`).

## Done

Return ticket id, what changed (note vs description vs fields), resulting
status, and browse URL when known. Stop — do not implement product code
unless the user added an explicit implement verb.
